{"name":"Crown of Ash","hex":"#a1a9a9","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"crown","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A royal, imperial or princely headdress; a diadem.","A wreath or band for the head, especially one given as reward of victory or a mark of honor."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Of, related to, or pertaining to a crown.","Of, related to, pertaining to the top of a tree or trees."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/crown"},{"term":"ash","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Symbol","definitions":["ISO 639-3 language code for Abishira."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The solid remains of a fire.","The nonaqueous remains of a material subjected to any complete oxidation process."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/ash"}],"entries":[{"title":"Crown","blocks":[{"text":"A crown is a traditional form of head adornment, or hat, worn by monarchs as a symbol of their power and dignity. A crown is often, by extension, a symbol of the monarch's government or items endorsed by it. The word itself is used, particularly in Commonwealth countries, as an abstract name for the monarchy itself as distinct from the individual who inhabits it. A specific type of crown is employed in heraldry under strict rules. Indeed, some monarchies never had a physical crown, just a heraldic representation, to wit the constitutional kingdom of Belgium."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/64/Saint_Edward%27s_Crown.jpg/330px-Saint_Edward%27s_Crown.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Crown"},{"title":"Ash","blocks":[{"text":"Ash is the solid remnants of fires. Specifically, ash refers to all non-aqueous, non-gaseous residues that remain after something burns. In analytical chemistry, to analyse the mineral and metal content of chemical samples, ash is the non-gaseous, non-liquid residue after complete combustion."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/09/Wood_ash.jpg/330px-Wood_ash.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ash"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b6/King_of_Persis_Ardashir_II_with_crown_1st_century_BCE.jpg/250px-King_of_Persis_Ardashir_II_with_crown_1st_century_BCE.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/b/b6/King_of_Persis_Ardashir_II_with_crown_1st_century_BCE.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b6/King_of_Persis_Ardashir_II_with_crown_1st_century_BCE.jpg/250px-King_of_Persis_Ardashir_II_with_crown_1st_century_BCE.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Crown of King of Persis Ardakhshir II, 1st century BC.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AKing_of_Persis_Ardashir_II_with_crown_1st_century_CE.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a0/Iron_Crown.JPG/500px-Iron_Crown.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a0/Iron_Crown.JPG/1280px-Iron_Crown.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a0/Iron_Crown.JPG/500px-Iron_Crown.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":" The Iron Crown of Lombardy. ","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AIron_Crown.JPG"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/8b/Crown_of_Kingdom_of_Nepal_%22%E0%A4%B6%E0%A5%8D%E0%A4%B0%E0%A5%80%E0%A4%AA%E0%A5%87%E0%A4%9A%22.jpg/120px-Crown_of_Kingdom_of_Nepal_%22%E0%A4%B6%E0%A5%8D%E0%A4%B0%E0%A5%80%E0%A4%AA%E0%A5%87%E0%A4%9A%22.jpg?utm_source=en.wikiped